>
  <p class="lead-para">
    <strong>The real career options after 12th except engineering are not a list of jobs. They are 14 entrance doors, and each one closes on a fixed date, asks for exact Class 12 subjects, or caps your age.</strong>
    Design, the IISERs, law, IPM, B.Arch, pilot training, the merchant navy and the NDA all sit outside a B.Tech. Pick by your subjects and your date of birth first, then by the date. The door that fits those three things is the one that can build a high-value skill portfolio, unlock stronger income options and move you toward earlier financial freedom.
  </p>

